h a `<td colSpan={4}` containing 'No products found.' centered.\",\"dependencies\":[1],\"context_files\":[\"src/types/product.ts\"],\"acceptance\":\"Component renders a table with 4 columns, formats price as USD currency, shows Edit and Delete buttons per row, shows empty state message when array is empty.\",\"verification\":\"compilation\"},{\"id\":5,\"domain\":\"frontend\",\"developer\":\"frontend-developer\",\"action\":\"modify\",\"target\":\"src/App.tsx\",\"description\":\"Replace the default App component content. Import `useState`, `useEffect` from React; import `Product`, `ProductFormData` from `./types/product`; import all four api functions from `./services/api`; import `ProductForm` from `./components/ProductForm`; import `ProductList` from `./components/ProductList`. State: `products: Product[]` (empty array default), `editingProduct: Product | null` (null default), `loading: boolean` (true default), `error: string | null` (null default). `useEffect` on mount: call `getProducts()`, set products on success, set error message on catch, set loading false in finally. `handleAdd(data: ProductFormData)`: call `addProduct(data)`, then re-fetch products via `getProducts()` and update state. `handleEdit(product: Product)`: set `editingProduct` to the product. `handleUpdate(data: ProductFormData)`: if `editingProduct` exists, call `updateProduct(editingProduct.id, data)`, re-fetch products, set `editingProduct` to null. `handleDelete(id: string)`: call `deleteProduct(id)`, re-fetch products. Render: an `<h1>` 'Product Management'. If loading show a `<p>Loading...</p>`. If error show `<p className='error'>{error}</p>`. A section with heading 'Add Product' (or 'Edit Product' if `editingProduct` is not null) containing `<ProductForm>` with `onSubmit` wired to `handleAdd` or `handleUpdate` based on `editingProduct`, pass `initialData` as `{name: editingProduct.name, price: String(editingProduct.price), category: editingProduct.category}` when editing, `isEditing={editingProduct !== null}`, `onCancel={() => setEditingProduct(null)}`. Below the form render `<ProductList products={products} onEdit={handleEdit} onDelete={handleDelete} />`.\",\"dependencies\":[2,3,4],\"context_files\":[\"src/types/product.ts\",\"src/services/api.ts\",\"src/components/ProductForm.tsx\",\"src/components/ProductList.tsx\"],\"acceptance\":\"App loads products on mount, AddProduct form adds a new row to the table, Edit button populates form with existing data and updates on submit, Delete button removes a row, Cancel resets to add mode.\",\"verification\":\"compilation\"},{\"id\":6,\"domain\":\"styling\",\"developer\":\"styling-developer\",\"action\":\"modify\",\"target\":\"src/App.css\",\"description\":\"Replace or append CSS rules to style the CRUD interface. Add rules for: `h1` — `font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;`. A `.form-group` class with `margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem;`. A `.error-text` class with `color: #dc2626; font-size: 0.875rem;`. A `.error` class (app-level error banner) with `color: #dc2626; background: #fee2e2; padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 0.375rem;`. Table styles: `table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }`, `th, td { padding: 0.75rem 1rem; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; }`, `th { background: #f9fafb; font-weight: 600; }`. Button styles: `button { padding: 0.375rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 0.375rem; border: none; cursor: pointer; margin-right: 0.5rem; }`, `.btn-edit { background: #3b82f6; color: white; }`, `.btn-delete { background: #ef4444; color: white; }`, `.btn-submit { background: #10b981; color: white; padding: 0.5rem 1.25rem; }`, `.btn-cancel { background: #6b7280; color: white; padding: 0.5rem 1.25rem; }`. Ensure form inputs get `border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 0.375rem; padding: 0.375rem 0.75rem; width: 100%;` and focus ring `outline: 2px solid #3b82f6;`.\",\"dependencies\":[5],\"context_files\":[\"src/App.tsx\",\"src/c